    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90465.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "No. No. No. Maybe public service in a broad sense. My mom and dad were public servants. My dad was a great teacher and coach. They worked on the slopes of Mount Rainier, teaching kids how to restore alpine meadows. We were always very outdoor oriented and they were very oriented to protecting our state. So public service writ large, but not politics. I really didn't think in these terms at all till I was in my late 30s. And Trudy and I got upset because we finally passed a school bond on the seventh try because we were going to have to double shift our schools, our high school. And then as soon as we passed it through kind of a miracle, uh... the chowder heads in the legislature cut the funding formula in half so i get angry about that and sometimes that's a good motivator so i decided instead of throw rocks from the outside i ran for the decision in and one of republican red district and the rest of history as they say over in central washington",
