    "turn_idx": 101,
    "turn_text": "Yes. Probably more than I imagined about the difference of the ability to actually move the needle. So, you know, take climate change, for instance. So I worked day and night to pass climate change legislation. We got it through the House. The Senate stalled. And that was disappointing. But now I have been able to, through executive action with the stroke of my pan, create a limitation on the amount of carbon pollution in the state of Washington. So it's the only one in the United States that has been created by executive action. It's pursuant to our state clean air law. And I have been able to tell my citizens that we're putting a cap on the amount of carbon pollution that comes out of our smokestacks and tailpipes. And that's a signal achievement and it only happened because I had that executive authority to do that. We've been able to pass",
