    "turn_idx": 111,
    "turn_text": "It's really the key to maximizing all renewable energy sources, because almost all renewable energy sources are intermittent. So you've got a lot of energy when you can't use it. So storage really is the alpha and omega of research right now. And Washington is leading the way, both in energy companies and in research. We've also established a Clean Energy Research Institute. at our colleges which are turn out some gangbusters, new developments both in storage and integration. Our companies are also specializing in development of software to be able to integrate renewable energy into the grid. So we see this as a huge economic growth opportunity for my state and we were only been able to do that because I've been in the governor's office to be able to move that forward.",
