  {
    "episode_id": 90465,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90465.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 120,
    "turn_text": "Well, I would say the Gingrich revolution was damaging to the democratic institution of the US Congress. And the reason is, is that he saw a weapon to drive disrespect for the United States Congress. He believed that the higher the disrespect number was for the US Congress, the more likely it was that the that the party in power which was the democratic party that time would be thrown out so since then there has been sort of uh... an industry built on belittling congress and belittling the opposition in their motivations and their personal attributes, which has made it a more acidic environment from a partisan standpoint.",
