    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "The success of political fundraising correlates with electoral outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
      {
        "text": "Dark money contributions represent a significant and effective resource for political campaigns.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker believes the Governor's Association leadership has influence or responsibility over candidate funding strategies.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "A financial disadvantage in fundraising puts candidates at risk of losing elections.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The Democratic Party lacks comparable organizational capacity in fundraising relative to the Republican Party.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Clarification Request (Specific)"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 90465,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90465.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 161,
    "turn_text": "Well, Republicans are going to spend more money than we do. That's just a fact of life. It was written in the evolutionary script, I suppose, and you just got to live with that. But I'm confident our candidates will be adequately funded, in part because we're so dedicated to this task. Look, we've understood that electing Democratic governors is not just important for our states. but is now important to unlock the US House of Representatives by stopping the gerrymandering that has so poisoned that body politic. And so we now are educating our donors. And because of this, I think we've doubled our individual contribution level from individual donors since I've been Vice Chair of the DGA. We're going to continue to build that. People are responding. I've been flying around the country when I can spare a moment from my duties as governor, talking to these donors who have been very active in Senate, US Senate races or US House races, but here to four have not been in the governor's races. They are now getting engaged because they understand the fundamental a pivot we have to make to win these state house races. Look, we were asleep at the switch for 10 years. Myself included to some degree. We were playing in house races, center races, but we have not been adequately funding state legislative races. I couldn't agree more. Mayors races, governors races, and the Koch brothers have been frankly 10 years ahead of us. We are catching up very rapidly and the organization I lead is going to be fundamental to that effort.",
