    "turn_text": "i think what i what i would say is to the to the administration is looked at tides of history are moving towards more equality, more openness. You are now in the wrong side of the tides of history by banning transgendered people from the military. That is a backwards approach, and you are on the wrong side of history if you want to go back and try to put marijuana back in this a broken bottle and make it a crime again you're just on the wrong side of history the culture in the community is moving in these directions and in my state they have been successful on both of those regards and I we haven't talked about this and you know we were very welcoming state we're welcoming people of whatever gender Whatever orientation, we welcome refugees. That's why I ran down the airport when I heard that the president was going to bar refugees. I went to CTAC right away. I'm proud that our state was one of the first, if not the first, to win in law in a lawsuit against this administration. And I think it's just another indication that they're going the wrong way",
